  "_comment": "What the builder installs in the example house, beyond walls and floors: kitchen cabinets and sink, bathroom fixtures, electrical devices, heating and ventilation. No loose furniture: the app is for building and renovating. Built by tools/house-model/build_house.py; every object is clickable and opens the item (data/items.yaml) it is sold as. A piece names its item, and a part may name its own. Parts are in local metres: at = [u, v] centre on the plan, y = bottom height, size = [width u, depth v, height]. For counting, a part with unit: true is one unit of its item (else one per placement), and an item measured by length sums the widths of its parts with length: true. A piece's front faces +v; a placement turns it by rotate degrees (0 front south, 90 west, 180 north, 270 east) and puts its origin at plan [x, z]; wall devices have their origin on the wall face.",
